  "markdown": "[image: decorative ornamental border]\n\n[logo]\n\n[image: dense horizontal line of dark stripes]\n\nVALUE AT MATURITY £101,800-00. [logo: D.C.O.] Due 21st January 1965 [stamp: BARCLAYS BANK D.C.O. REGISTERED COMMERCIAL BANK WITH WHICH IS AMALGAMATED] No. 301 THE NATIONAL BANK OF SOUTH AFRICA LIMITED\n\nHead Office in South Africa\nJOHANNESBURG, [e-signature] 25th Jn\n\n# NEGOTIABLE CERTIFICATE OF DEPOSIT\n\nThis certifies that there has been deposited with Barclays Bank D.C.O. the sum of R100,000-00 (One hundred thousand Rand) payable to *the Bearer of this Certificate *the Order of\n\n180 days after date hereof together with interest at the rate of 3.65 per cent per annum.\n\nThe amount of the deposit and the interest thereon will be repaid upon presentation of this Certificate at the Johannesburg Branch of Barclays Bank D.C.O. on or after 21st January 1965 on which date interest will cease.\n\n[signature] General Manager\n\n[signature] Chief Accountant\n\nN.B.—THE ISSUE AND NEGOTIATION OF THIS CERTIFICATE ARE SUBJECT TO THE CONDITIONS PRINTED ON THE BACK HEREOF.\n* DELETE WHICHEVER IS INAPPLICABLE.\n\n[image]\n\n<figure type=\"PHOTOGRAPH\">SOUTH AFRICA R4 SUID-AFRIKA SOUTH AFRICA R1 SOUTH AFRICA R20 SUID-AFRIKA\n\n\n<description>Black-and-white image of a vertical strip of three South African stamps on a white background. The top stamp shows a coat of arms above a large \"R4\" denomination with \"SOUTH AFRICA\" and \"SUID-AFRIKA\" text around it. The middle stamp shows a coat of arms above \"R1\" with \"SOUTH AFRICA\" text. The bottom stamp shows a coat of arms above \"R20\" with \"SUID-AFRIKA\" text. The stamps are partially cropped at the top and bottom edges, with faint decorative borders and blurred printed text visible.</description></figure>\n\n[signature]\n\n<!-- doc_id=parse-01m7ry4z0m652twt3br7dn95zq -->",
